1
00:00:01,420 --> 00:00:04,710
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:33,930
[GONZO] We can all eat
together in here.

3
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:36,810
My goodness.

4
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:40,680
The great hall has
certainly seen better days.

5
00:01:40,770 --> 00:01:42,310
You want me to fix it?

6
00:01:42,390 --> 00:01:43,440
If you would.

7
00:01:47,230 --> 00:01:49,900
[HAGURE] Oof. This'll be one
heck of a job.

8
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:53,570
What?

9
00:01:55,070 --> 00:01:56,450
[HAGURE] Mm...

10
00:01:58,450 --> 00:01:59,540
[RIGHT] Uh?

11
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:01,750
-It vanished.
-A clean slate.

12
00:02:05,460 --> 00:02:07,130
[HAGURE] Mm...

13
00:02:08,250 --> 00:02:10,050
[all gasp]

14
00:02:18,510 --> 00:02:19,600
Glad that's settled,

15
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:21,390
'cause I'm starting to get
real hungry.

16
00:02:22,430 --> 00:02:24,560
It's like the floor
was never damaged.

17
00:02:25,190 --> 00:02:26,480
[DERA] What?

18
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:27,900
How does it work?

19
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:30,070
-Let me introduce my daemons.
-[BOTH] Huh?

20
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:31,360
Meet Black and White.

21
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:33,860
On my left shoulder,
I've got Whiteout.

22
00:02:33,940 --> 00:02:35,200
And Ink is on the right.

23
00:02:36,030 --> 00:02:38,740
If I wanna fix something,
Whiteout erases for me.

24
00:02:38,820 --> 00:02:41,160
Then Ink draws in new stuff.

25
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:45,210
You have to be imaginative
and observant to use them.

26
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:47,130
That's why an artist
is the perfect person

27
00:02:47,210 --> 00:02:48,500
to command these daemons.

28
00:02:48,590 --> 00:02:49,670
You're an artist?

29
00:02:49,750 --> 00:02:53,380
I work as a mangaka.
I'm Hikaru Hagure!

30
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:54,590
[both spit]

31
00:02:54,670 --> 00:02:56,470
Oh, and please don't mind
the spitting.

32
00:02:56,550 --> 00:02:59,390
Believe it or not, that's how
these two show affection.

33
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:01,600
[YURU] "Mangaka?"
What's that mean?

34
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:03,520
Huh? I know you!

35
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:05,060
They made a bunch of movies

36
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:07,020
outta the stories you published.
I've seen them!

37
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:08,690
Thanks for your support!

38
00:03:08,770 --> 00:03:11,400
I'm lucky to make a good living
as an artist.

39
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:13,400
Hagure is just
a pen name, though.

40
00:03:13,490 --> 00:03:15,820
My real name is actually
Hikaru Kagemori.

41
00:03:15,900 --> 00:03:17,410
A pen name?

42
00:03:17,490 --> 00:03:18,780
An alias.

43
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:20,830
[HAGURE] Our family's got
a ruthless reputation,

44
00:03:20,910 --> 00:03:23,160
so I figured it was smart
to use a pseudonym.

45
00:03:23,250 --> 00:03:25,500
You know,
to avoid controversy.

46
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:28,000
So the great mangaka's
a Kagemori, too?

47
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:30,750
To be specific,
the three of us are brothers.

48
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:32,420
I'm the oldest of the bunch.

49
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:34,300
I'm the middle child.

50
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:37,090
And I'm the kid brother,
of course.

51
00:03:37,180 --> 00:03:39,180
Really? Weird.

52
00:03:39,260 --> 00:03:41,260
Seriously?
You're the youngest one?

53
00:03:41,350 --> 00:03:42,810
The baby.

54
00:03:42,890 --> 00:03:45,220
Let me explain.
You're probably wondering

55
00:03:45,310 --> 00:03:48,060
why we don't really look
anything alike. [laughs]

56
00:03:48,150 --> 00:03:49,270
Three different moms.

57
00:03:49,350 --> 00:03:50,560
As the eldest,

58
00:03:50,650 --> 00:03:53,150
Hagure will one day
be the head of our clan.

59
00:03:53,230 --> 00:03:55,400
So you'd be wise to stay
in his good graces.

60
00:03:55,490 --> 00:03:56,900
No way, dude!

61
00:03:56,990 --> 00:03:59,530
I am not cut out to lead
a sketchy clan like this.

62
00:03:59,610 --> 00:04:01,240
All I want is a peaceful life

63
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:04,080
where I get to draw cute little
manga stories until I die.

64
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:06,790
I still have a decent
set of morals, you know.

65
00:04:06,870 --> 00:04:08,000
Unlike you guys.

66
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:09,330
I kinda thought

67
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:11,080
that the more screwed up
the creator was,

68
00:04:11,170 --> 00:04:13,170
the more interesting
their stories turned out.

69
00:04:13,250 --> 00:04:15,210
You're stereotyping.

70
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:17,630
[DERA] Hm... Mr. Mangaka,

71
00:04:17,720 --> 00:04:19,300
you may have
repaired everything,

72
00:04:19,380 --> 00:04:21,260
but your fixes
are in monochrome.

73
00:04:21,340 --> 00:04:23,310
Are you really sure
this is safe?

74
00:04:23,390 --> 00:04:24,930
There's nothing to worry about.

75
00:04:25,010 --> 00:04:28,230
The surrounding colors
will eventually bleed into it.

76
00:04:28,310 --> 00:04:30,520
You won't be able
to tell the difference.

77
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:33,770
Ugh... The pillar details
are way off, though.

78
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:35,610
I made it look too clean.

79
00:04:35,690 --> 00:04:37,860
The edges are sharp,
but given the building's age,

80
00:04:37,940 --> 00:04:40,570
they should've been
smoothed over by time and touch.

81
00:04:40,650 --> 00:04:42,280
What an absolute
amateur mistake.

82
00:04:42,370 --> 00:04:45,080
[grunts] And the floor's wrong!
The tatami mats have seen

83
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:46,410
a ton of foot traffic
over the years

84
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:48,700
and should look way more
beaten up than this!

85
00:04:48,790 --> 00:04:50,370
These are practically brand new!

86
00:04:50,460 --> 00:04:53,040
Ah, man. What was I thinking?

87
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:56,340
I'm redoing this immediately!

88
00:04:59,510 --> 00:05:00,840
[JIN]
Can we eat breakfast first?

89
00:05:03,850 --> 00:05:05,600
[SERVANT] Thank you all
for your patience.

90
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:07,600
Breakfast is served.

91
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:09,940
Please, sit wherever you'd like.

92
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:11,480
Let's keep this casual.

93
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:13,810
We're an upstart clan,

94
00:05:13,900 --> 00:05:15,810
so we're not overly concerned
with traditions

95
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:18,940
or things like seating order
and etiquette at the moment.

96
00:05:19,030 --> 00:05:20,610
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two!
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four!

97
00:05:20,690 --> 00:05:22,280
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two!
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four!

98
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:23,700
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two!
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four!

99
00:05:23,780 --> 00:05:25,530
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two!
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four!

100
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:27,200
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two!
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four!

101
00:05:28,750 --> 00:05:30,500
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two!
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four!

102
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:32,120
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two!
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four!

103
00:05:32,210 --> 00:05:33,670
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two!
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four!

104
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:35,000
Please sit.

105
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:37,250
Oh, thank you.

106
00:05:37,340 --> 00:05:39,960
[TSUGAI 3]
Left, right, left, right.

107
00:05:40,050 --> 00:05:42,010
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two!
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four!

108
00:05:42,090 --> 00:05:43,430
-[TSUGAI 1] One, two!
-[TSUGAI 2] Three, four!

109
00:05:43,510 --> 00:05:46,640
What's this? You're preparing
seats for us as well?

110
00:05:46,720 --> 00:05:49,350
You do realize we don't consume
human food.

111
00:05:49,430 --> 00:05:51,520
Sure, but you're
still our guests.

112
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:54,060
And we treat
all of our guests equally.

113
00:06:02,860 --> 00:06:05,910
So, you knew
Mr. Big Brother was here.

114
00:06:05,990 --> 00:06:07,280
You care to tell us how?

115
00:06:07,370 --> 00:06:08,990
Nah, it's a secret.

116
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:12,120
-Mmm.
-[JIN] Curious.

117
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:15,250
The mansion was attacked
by multiple daemons last night.

118
00:06:16,080 --> 00:06:19,090
I assume that Higashi Village
sent them to kill us.

119
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:21,170
[DERA] Uh, don't ask me.

120
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:22,210
[HAGURE] Aw, man.

121
00:06:22,630 --> 00:06:24,630
So much for having
a lighthearted breakfast.

122
00:06:24,720 --> 00:06:27,430
I didn't order an attack
on Kagemori headquarters,

123
00:06:27,510 --> 00:06:28,760
if that's what you're implying.

124
00:06:29,470 --> 00:06:31,520
[JIN] It happened
right after Yuru arrived.

125
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:34,100
Don't you think
that timing is suspicious?

126
00:06:34,190 --> 00:06:35,520
Mm? Whoa!

127
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:38,020
[ASA] My brother is eating
in front of me.

128
00:06:38,650 --> 00:06:40,770
And from what I understand,

129
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:43,820
members of the Tadera clan
can slip through barriers.

130
00:06:44,450 --> 00:06:46,110
Our own barriers, sure.

131
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:47,700
Not ones that belong
to other people.

132
00:06:47,780 --> 00:06:51,080
[ASA] Oh, my gosh, my brother
is drinking miso soup.

133
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:53,870
-That's good!
-More importantly, Asa.

134
00:06:53,950 --> 00:06:55,870
Have the Kagemoris been
mistreating you?

135
00:06:55,960 --> 00:06:57,790
You can save your concern.

136
00:06:57,880 --> 00:07:00,130
They've fed me well
and treated me with kindness

137
00:07:00,210 --> 00:07:01,590
ever since I came to them.

138
00:07:01,670 --> 00:07:03,050
This manor's a fortress.

139
00:07:03,130 --> 00:07:04,590
I'm safe from assassin attacks

140
00:07:04,670 --> 00:07:06,340
as long as I remain
on the grounds.

141
00:07:06,430 --> 00:07:09,260
Though last night's raid
was obviously an exception.

142
00:07:09,350 --> 00:07:11,220
And take one step
outside the gates,

143
00:07:11,310 --> 00:07:12,890
and enemies are all over you.

144
00:07:12,970 --> 00:07:15,640
[SAKURAZAWA] I don't approve
of her leaving the manor,

145
00:07:15,730 --> 00:07:18,360
but when our infirmary
is insufficient,

146
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:21,110
she's forced to visit
outside clinics for treatment.

147
00:07:21,730 --> 00:07:24,400
Her safety and security
are always an issue

148
00:07:24,490 --> 00:07:25,940
whenever that happens.

149
00:07:26,030 --> 00:07:27,990
That's how
the Higashi Village assassins

150
00:07:28,070 --> 00:07:29,200
managed to get me.

151
00:07:29,530 --> 00:07:31,080
They timed their attack
for when I was recovering

152
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:32,240
at the hospital.

153
00:07:32,620 --> 00:07:34,870
Whoa, recovering?
You must've been seriously sick.

154
00:07:35,910 --> 00:07:37,670
[ASA] Thanks to you.

155
00:07:37,750 --> 00:07:40,000
The stress of constantly
being targeted

156
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:42,670
by Higashi Village agents
gave me a gastric ulcer,

157
00:07:42,750 --> 00:07:45,460
meaning my stomach felt like
I'd swallowed battery acid.

158
00:07:45,550 --> 00:07:47,550
[DERA] Hey,
don't look at me like that.

159
00:07:47,630 --> 00:07:49,510
I wasn't the one
giving the orders.

160
00:07:49,590 --> 00:07:52,100
[ASA] Also, hospitals are full
of innocent bystanders,

161
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:55,060
so it's a real pain for everyone
when assassins show up.

162
00:07:55,140 --> 00:07:57,600
Stop sending them.

163
00:07:57,690 --> 00:08:00,440
I told you,
it's not my fault, I swear.

164
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:02,610
Please blame
the extremists instead.

165
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:05,440
For what it's worth, I'm sorry
they've caused problems.

166
00:08:05,530 --> 00:08:06,610
[Dera gasps]

167
00:08:06,690 --> 00:08:10,070
Hey, hold on.
You must have insurance!

168
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:12,160
Hospitals will
bleed you dry without it.

169
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:14,240
So, how did you become
an official citizen?

170
00:08:14,330 --> 00:08:16,950
I gotta figure something out
for Yuru.

171
00:08:17,540 --> 00:08:20,580
I haven't been able to register
with the government yet.

172
00:08:20,670 --> 00:08:22,540
[DERA] Eesh.
That must be tough.

173
00:08:22,630 --> 00:08:25,550
It should have been simple,
since my mother is from here.

174
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:28,970
In theory, all I needed to do
was register as her daughter.

175
00:08:29,970 --> 00:08:34,050
But then somebody attacked her
and she and my father vanished,

176
00:08:34,140 --> 00:08:35,180
leaving no trace.

177
00:08:35,260 --> 00:08:36,560
What?

178
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:38,390
You mean your parents
are missing?

179
00:08:38,480 --> 00:08:39,600
So she says.

180
00:08:39,690 --> 00:08:41,150
Oh, boy. Look, kid,

181
00:08:41,230 --> 00:08:44,020
I know I'm technically
on Higashi Village's side,

182
00:08:44,110 --> 00:08:45,860
but I promise this is the first

183
00:08:45,940 --> 00:08:47,610
I've heard about
them disappearing.

184
00:08:47,690 --> 00:08:48,950
At the very least,

185
00:08:49,030 --> 00:08:50,860
I doubt anyone that I know
in the community

186
00:08:50,950 --> 00:08:53,240
would be behind
whatever happened to them.

187
00:08:53,910 --> 00:08:55,990
And you really
expect us to take you,

188
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:57,580
an enemy agent, at your word?

189
00:08:57,660 --> 00:08:59,830
While it's my duty
to kill anybody

190
00:08:59,910 --> 00:09:01,500
who intrudes on our territory,

191
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:04,340
I don't attack people
for no reason.

192
00:09:04,420 --> 00:09:07,760
And I don't agree with
any of the radicals who do.

193
00:09:08,380 --> 00:09:09,840
I'm not even armed!

194
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:11,930
I showed up on your doorstep
in good faith

195
00:09:12,010 --> 00:09:13,970
looking for Yuru, not a fight.

196
00:09:14,050 --> 00:09:16,850
Have you considered that maybe
Kagemori extremists

197
00:09:16,930 --> 00:09:17,970
are the ones to blame?

198
00:09:18,310 --> 00:09:20,430
I've heard your clan
isn't a monolith, either.

199
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:23,020
You've got your own bad apples.

200
00:09:24,690 --> 00:09:26,570
The twins have been reunited.

201
00:09:27,070 --> 00:09:28,150
I'm wondering,

202
00:09:28,230 --> 00:09:30,240
"What is it you plan
to do with them?"

203
00:09:33,030 --> 00:09:34,620
[Gonzo exhales]

204
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:36,870
[GONZO] Each time
twins like you are born,

205
00:09:36,950 --> 00:09:38,700
the world is thrown into chaos.

206
00:09:39,870 --> 00:09:42,710
Humanity is better off
without Break or Seal.

207
00:09:45,790 --> 00:09:47,630
It would be best for everyone

208
00:09:47,710 --> 00:09:50,050
if Asa and Yuru
were the final set of twins,

209
00:09:50,130 --> 00:09:52,420
and their backwards village
were simply destroyed

210
00:09:52,510 --> 00:09:53,880
once and for all.

211
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:58,180
It's a wretched place
filled with wretched people,

212
00:09:58,260 --> 00:10:00,930
consumed by outdated values
and dreams of conquering

213
00:10:01,020 --> 00:10:02,100
the rest of us.

214
00:10:02,890 --> 00:10:04,480
They are too great a threat.

215
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:06,270
And since we share their blood,

216
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:07,980
it's our responsibility
to make sure

217
00:10:08,070 --> 00:10:09,650
they're taken care of.

218
00:10:11,030 --> 00:10:12,650
[ASUMA] I disagree, Father.

219
00:10:13,490 --> 00:10:15,990
I believe that those chosen
to wield great power

220
00:10:16,070 --> 00:10:17,950
should use their gifts
to govern the world

221
00:10:18,030 --> 00:10:19,410
and ensure peace.

222
00:10:19,490 --> 00:10:22,120
They were granted
their abilities by the gods,

223
00:10:22,210 --> 00:10:23,460
were they not?

224
00:10:23,540 --> 00:10:26,290
The onus is on them
to use it wisely.

225
00:10:26,380 --> 00:10:28,710
I'm guessing you think
your clan is best suited

226
00:10:28,790 --> 00:10:30,590
to control that power.

227
00:10:30,670 --> 00:10:33,760
[ASUMA] Yes. The village
that produces Break and Seal

228
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:35,630
should be allowed to live on.

229
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:38,890
We mustn't reject
their very existence.

230
00:10:38,970 --> 00:10:40,890
That said,
they need to be controlled

231
00:10:40,970 --> 00:10:42,680
by suitable overseers.

232
00:10:42,770 --> 00:10:44,890
Like our organization.

233
00:10:47,650 --> 00:10:48,730
Left and Right?

234
00:10:48,820 --> 00:10:50,570
Go on.

235
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:52,940
Earlier, I asked if the twins
were cursed

236
00:10:53,030 --> 00:10:54,780
to throw the world into chaos.

237
00:10:54,860 --> 00:10:56,910
You denied it
without hesitation.

238
00:10:57,820 --> 00:10:59,740
You said it's those
who wish to abuse the power

239
00:10:59,830 --> 00:11:02,750
for their own ends who wind up
causing problems, yes?

240
00:11:03,660 --> 00:11:05,080
You were certain.

241
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:07,830
And so quick to tell me
we weren't at fault.

242
00:11:07,920 --> 00:11:10,170
Took a massive weight
off my shoulders.

243
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:14,220
You made me feel like it's
all right for me to just live.

244
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:19,470
So thank you.

245
00:11:27,480 --> 00:11:29,650
I appreciate the meal.

246
00:11:31,150 --> 00:11:32,270
This girl...

247
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:34,530
She apologizes for everything.

248
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:37,360
I'm not about to forgive her
for what she did to the village,

249
00:11:37,450 --> 00:11:39,160
but I've seen her apologizing

250
00:11:39,240 --> 00:11:40,620
for things
that aren't her fault.

251
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:43,290
Who convinced her
she needs to live

252
00:11:43,370 --> 00:11:45,620
with her shame
hanging around her neck?

253
00:11:45,710 --> 00:11:48,920
Who convinced her that
every little thing is her fault?

254
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,500
Why should we be forced
to live in secret?

255
00:11:52,590 --> 00:11:55,840
Just because we're the twins
in some ancient prophecy?

256
00:11:56,550 --> 00:11:57,970
Why should anybody but us

257
00:11:58,050 --> 00:11:59,970
get to say
how we live our lives?

258
00:12:00,050 --> 00:12:01,050
[Asa gasps softly]

259
00:12:04,770 --> 00:12:08,140
You had agreed your clan
isn't a monolith, either.

260
00:12:08,230 --> 00:12:10,400
I'm sure the extremists
will hear this,

261
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:12,610
and that doesn't bother me
one bit.

262
00:12:13,690 --> 00:12:14,730
And Dera...

263
00:12:14,820 --> 00:12:17,110
You can report this
to Higashi, too.

264
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:20,110
Because if no one wants
to give me any peace,

265
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:23,330
fine! I'm not gonna live
my life on the run!

266
00:12:23,410 --> 00:12:25,580
And I've got
no reason to hide!

267
00:12:25,660 --> 00:12:29,750
I don't care if you're
from Higashi or the Kagemoris.

268
00:12:29,830 --> 00:12:31,130
I'm not afraid.

269
00:12:31,210 --> 00:12:33,710
If you want my head,
come and get it!

270
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:35,170
Just know...

271
00:12:35,250 --> 00:12:38,130
After I beat them
black and blue,

272
00:12:38,220 --> 00:12:41,390
I'll squeeze them for
all the information they've got.

273
00:12:41,470 --> 00:12:43,300
Whoa. Slow down, there.

274
00:12:44,050 --> 00:12:46,930
How dare you be such an idiot!

275
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:53,730
[ASA] How dare you be
such an idiot!

276
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:55,440
[Yuru stutters]

277
00:12:58,530 --> 00:12:59,740
[Yuru grunts]

278
00:12:59,820 --> 00:13:02,700
Hey, hold on!
Who are you calling an idiot?

279
00:13:02,780 --> 00:13:04,080
[ASA] "No reason to hide?"

280
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:05,780
That's the dumbest thing
I've ever heard!

281
00:13:05,870 --> 00:13:08,250
You're lucky!
You can say stuff like that

282
00:13:08,330 --> 00:13:10,330
because you don't know
what it's like being hounded

283
00:13:10,410 --> 00:13:13,210
by assassins night and day
for your whole life.

284
00:13:13,290 --> 00:13:16,290
But I don't want you to suffer
like I have all these years!

285
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:18,720
So run! Or lay low somewhere!

286
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:20,300
Don't throw your life away!

287
00:13:20,380 --> 00:13:22,010
What's this kid's deal?

288
00:13:22,090 --> 00:13:24,930
Is he the type who only knows
"go big or go home?"

289
00:13:25,010 --> 00:13:26,050
I'd say so.

290
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:29,140
[ASA] You two, help me get it
through his thick skull... Uh?

291
00:13:29,230 --> 00:13:30,890
Ah, but as his daemons,

292
00:13:30,980 --> 00:13:33,650
we must always do
as our master says, lass!

293
00:13:33,730 --> 00:13:36,940
Should trouble befall us,
we've no choice but to fight!

294
00:13:37,020 --> 00:13:39,400
You don't seem too broken up
about that.

295
00:13:39,490 --> 00:13:41,530
I really don't see the problem.

296
00:13:41,610 --> 00:13:43,910
You've been dealing with this
alone for way too long.

297
00:13:43,990 --> 00:13:45,410
Why don't you
let your big brother

298
00:13:45,490 --> 00:13:47,580
take some of the heat off you
for a change?

299
00:13:47,660 --> 00:13:48,660
You're with him?

300
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:51,870
We have the most kind-hearted
of masters, do we not?

301
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:53,120
Hold on!

302
00:13:54,710 --> 00:13:57,960
Obviously, I know
that his heart is kind.

303
00:13:58,050 --> 00:13:59,420
I get it.

304
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:01,130
[Dera breathes uneasily]

305
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:02,590
[Yuru groans softly]

306
00:14:02,670 --> 00:14:04,300
Tell me, Yuru.

307
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:06,850
Would you not consider joining
the Kagemoris

308
00:14:06,930 --> 00:14:08,180
and coming to live with us?

309
00:14:08,260 --> 00:14:09,970
You'll be safer here.

310
00:14:10,060 --> 00:14:11,930
And we'll make sure
you're comfortable.

311
00:14:12,020 --> 00:14:14,810
You'll want for nothing
under our roof. So?

312
00:14:14,900 --> 00:14:17,480
-Not a chance.
-[GONZO] That was quick.

313
00:14:17,570 --> 00:14:19,070
Of course.

314
00:14:19,150 --> 00:14:22,150
You called Higashi and all
of its people wretched before.

315
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:24,610
But that's where
I was born and raised.

316
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:26,280
Those are my friends.

317
00:14:27,080 --> 00:14:29,490
I respect that you have
your own way of thinking,

318
00:14:29,580 --> 00:14:32,540
but just because I respect it
doesn't mean I accept it.

319
00:14:33,410 --> 00:14:35,080
I can't see eye to eye
with someone

320
00:14:35,170 --> 00:14:36,920
who did that to my home.

321
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:39,750
I know you're searching
for my parents,

322
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:41,170
and I'm grateful.

323
00:14:41,250 --> 00:14:42,920
You look out for your own,
like you should.

324
00:14:44,720 --> 00:14:45,970
I'll do the same, my way.

325
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:49,390
And for now, that means
working together with Dera.

326
00:14:49,470 --> 00:14:52,350
[sighs]
I'm with your sister, frankly.

327
00:14:52,430 --> 00:14:55,230
My life would be way easier
if you could try laying low.

328
00:14:55,850 --> 00:14:58,770
But for the moment at least,
I'm the kid's guardian.

329
00:14:58,860 --> 00:15:01,190
And that means supporting
whatever way he wants to live

330
00:15:01,270 --> 00:15:03,320
and making sure he stays safe.

331
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:05,200
You mind if we scram?

332
00:15:05,280 --> 00:15:06,450
About time we go.

333
00:15:07,410 --> 00:15:09,120
But thanks
for all the hospitality.

334
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,160
[GONZO] Hm.

335
00:15:11,910 --> 00:15:14,830
Hey, Left and Right...
Mr. Dera...

336
00:15:17,290 --> 00:15:18,460
[Yuru gasps softly]

337
00:15:20,210 --> 00:15:24,090
[ASA] I'm counting on you.
Please take care of my brother.

338
00:15:24,170 --> 00:15:25,720
Of course, lass.

339
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:27,090
[LEFT] Mm-hmm.

340
00:15:27,180 --> 00:15:28,550
Well, I'll try.

341
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:30,510
♪

342
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:41,690
I'm not able to walk you
any farther than here.

343
00:15:41,770 --> 00:15:43,480
That's where the barrier ends.

344
00:15:43,570 --> 00:15:45,490
If I take one step outside,

345
00:15:45,570 --> 00:15:48,610
I'm liable to being attacked
by those who want Break.

346
00:15:48,700 --> 00:15:51,620
[chuckles] Please be careful
out there, Yuru.

347
00:15:58,040 --> 00:15:59,460
[YURU] So that's how it is.

348
00:15:59,540 --> 00:16:01,880
She's trapped
inside these gates.

349
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:04,210
In the end,

350
00:16:04,300 --> 00:16:06,170
the only difference
between the manor

351
00:16:06,260 --> 00:16:08,220
and that cell is the size.

352
00:16:09,010 --> 00:16:10,930
-Oh, yeah. I almost forgot.
-[YURU] Hm?

353
00:16:11,010 --> 00:16:12,800
There's something
I wanna show you.

354
00:16:12,890 --> 00:16:13,930
Look here.

355
00:16:14,810 --> 00:16:15,930
[YURU] Huh?

356
00:16:16,350 --> 00:16:19,060
What? That looks exactly
like our parents!

357
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:20,650
It's the last thing
I have of them

358
00:16:20,730 --> 00:16:21,730
before they went missing.

359
00:16:21,810 --> 00:16:24,480
[YURU] But what is it?
A painting?

360
00:16:24,570 --> 00:16:26,940
[ASA] Uh, kind of like
a super realistic one,

361
00:16:27,030 --> 00:16:28,240
I suppose?

362
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:30,780
Let me show you how it works.

363
00:16:30,870 --> 00:16:32,160
Look up here.

364
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:34,080
-[phone camera clicks]
-[Yuru stammers]

365
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:35,370
[Yuru screams]

366
00:16:35,450 --> 00:16:37,620
[ASA] This technology
perfectly preserves

367
00:16:37,710 --> 00:16:39,830
a moment in time
to look back on later.

368
00:16:39,920 --> 00:16:41,880
I do not understand this at all,

369
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,210
but it's one of the
coolest things

370
00:16:43,290 --> 00:16:45,340
I've seen
in the world down here!

371
00:16:45,420 --> 00:16:46,710
[ASA] Perfect.

372
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:48,300
I took advantage
of the situation

373
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:49,550
to get a keepsake of him!

374
00:16:49,630 --> 00:16:50,970
A marvel!

375
00:16:51,050 --> 00:16:52,930
We humbly request to be
in a preserved image

376
00:16:53,010 --> 00:16:54,260
with our master as well!

377
00:16:54,350 --> 00:16:56,010
I'm sorry to say it...

378
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:57,060
[phone camera clicks]

379
00:16:57,480 --> 00:17:00,100
...but daemons don't usually
appear in photos.

380
00:17:00,190 --> 00:17:02,650
You're like spirits.
Elusive and all.

381
00:17:02,730 --> 00:17:04,570
They can be seen
on rare occasions

382
00:17:04,650 --> 00:17:07,190
if the lighting and timing
manage to line up just right.

383
00:17:07,280 --> 00:17:09,860
Ghost shows on TV
live for that stuff.

384
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:11,910
-[YURU] Asa...
-[ASA] Uh?

385
00:17:11,990 --> 00:17:15,120
If you don't mind,
could I take a look again?

386
00:17:15,910 --> 00:17:17,240
[ASA] Hm.

387
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:22,880
[Yuru chuckles] Their clothes
are from down here.

388
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:25,630
It's the first I've seen them
in ten years.

389
00:17:25,710 --> 00:17:28,380
They look strange.
It isn't bad at all.

390
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:31,340
I wonder where they are
and how they're doing.

391
00:17:32,050 --> 00:17:33,840
They are alive and healthy.

392
00:17:33,930 --> 00:17:35,390
I'm positive.

393
00:17:36,390 --> 00:17:38,560
I'll have this printed
and send it to you.

394
00:17:38,640 --> 00:17:40,560
So I can keep it?

395
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:43,100
Although, I'll need
to get your address for that.

396
00:17:43,190 --> 00:17:44,810
Where are you living these days?

397
00:17:44,900 --> 00:17:46,610
What's that place called again?

398
00:17:46,690 --> 00:17:48,190
Hang on, I know.

399
00:17:48,650 --> 00:17:49,860
It was Guntama!

400
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:51,030
Say what, now?

401
00:17:51,110 --> 00:17:52,320
This sucks.

402
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:54,200
I failed to take advantage
of the situation

403
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:55,740
to get my brother's address.

404
00:17:55,830 --> 00:17:57,580
Hey, Dera...

405
00:17:57,660 --> 00:17:59,700
I would give my address
to the Kagemoris,

406
00:17:59,790 --> 00:18:01,330
but I'd rather not die
in my sleep.

407
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:04,670
What if we receive information
regarding his parents?

408
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:06,340
It'd be nice to reach out.

409
00:18:06,420 --> 00:18:08,750
We won't ask for your address.

410
00:18:08,840 --> 00:18:11,050
But maybe an email,
or your number?

411
00:18:11,130 --> 00:18:12,170
Yeah, hell no.

412
00:18:12,260 --> 00:18:13,930
You think I don't know
how easy it is

413
00:18:14,010 --> 00:18:16,140
to doxx someone off
any random piece of info

414
00:18:16,220 --> 00:18:18,100
-you might have?
-[Jin grunts]

415
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:19,520
I'll grant you,

416
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:21,730
it would be nice to have a way
to contact each other

417
00:18:21,810 --> 00:18:23,350
if we ever need to.

418
00:18:23,440 --> 00:18:24,940
Carrier pigeons?

419
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:26,310
Walky-talkies?

420
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:28,820
Encrypted notes
at Shinjuku Station?

421
00:18:28,900 --> 00:18:29,860
Smoke signals!

422
00:18:30,150 --> 00:18:32,150
[ALL] That's in violation
of fire laws.

423
00:18:33,650 --> 00:18:36,700
[JIN] Oh, well. Come here
if you need anything.

424
00:18:37,780 --> 00:18:39,160
Sending me to a girls' bar?

425
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:41,870
It's one of the businesses
run by the Kagemoris.

426
00:18:42,500 --> 00:18:45,210
Just drop my name there
if you have a message for us.

427
00:18:45,290 --> 00:18:46,880
They should pass it along.

428
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:48,840
That will be
our point of contact.

429
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:50,800
[DERA] Hmm...

430
00:18:51,420 --> 00:18:53,090
That sounds good to me!

431
00:18:53,170 --> 00:18:56,590
[JIN] He's clearly gonna
go there and drink on my tab.

432
00:18:57,300 --> 00:18:58,890
[DERA] Anyway,
thanks for looking

433
00:18:58,970 --> 00:19:00,260
for the twins' parents.

434
00:19:00,350 --> 00:19:02,890
And thanks for
the lovely breakfast, too.

435
00:19:06,190 --> 00:19:07,400
Before you go...

436
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:11,780
They were heartbroken that day.

437
00:19:11,860 --> 00:19:13,570
Mom and Dad were inconsolable

438
00:19:13,650 --> 00:19:16,610
when they realized they couldn't
get you off the mountain.

439
00:19:16,700 --> 00:19:19,530
They did try, but Granny Yamaha
stopped them.

440
00:19:19,620 --> 00:19:21,870
It was all they could do
to escape that place

441
00:19:21,950 --> 00:19:24,160
with even one of their children.

442
00:19:24,250 --> 00:19:26,790
They wanted us
to leave as a family.

443
00:19:26,870 --> 00:19:28,330
So don't think for a second

444
00:19:28,420 --> 00:19:31,250
they were all right after
having to leave you behind!

445
00:19:31,340 --> 00:19:33,260
[Yuru breathes shakily]

446
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:45,480
[YURU] This trip was worth it,

447
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:47,310
if only just to hear that.

448
00:19:47,390 --> 00:19:48,650
[Asa sniffles]

449
00:19:50,770 --> 00:19:51,860
[YURU] Later.

450
00:19:56,780 --> 00:19:57,650
[Jin gasps]

451
00:19:58,530 --> 00:20:00,030
♪

452
00:20:14,050 --> 00:20:16,380
[ASA] Listen, brother.

453
00:20:16,460 --> 00:20:18,170
Take care of yourself.

454
00:20:21,350 --> 00:20:22,760
Till next time.

455
00:20:30,440 --> 00:20:32,570
[Yuru grunts, pants]

456
00:20:32,650 --> 00:20:35,070
[DERA] Uh... Hey, Yuru?

457
00:20:35,150 --> 00:20:36,650
[YURU] I messed up!

458
00:20:36,740 --> 00:20:38,650
She caught me off guard!

459
00:20:38,740 --> 00:20:40,910
If she were a bear,
I would be dead!

460
00:20:40,990 --> 00:20:42,660
Are you for real, kid?

461
00:20:44,580 --> 00:20:46,200
There's no doubt now.

462
00:20:46,660 --> 00:20:49,080
That's her. That's Asa.

463
00:20:49,660 --> 00:20:51,750
-[ASA] Listen...
-[YURU] Uh?

464
00:20:51,830 --> 00:20:54,000
Brother, take care of yourself.

465
00:20:54,090 --> 00:20:55,630
[Asa chuckles]

466
00:20:56,510 --> 00:20:57,760
[Yuru cries]

467
00:20:57,840 --> 00:21:00,470
That was her. That's my sister.

468
00:21:00,550 --> 00:21:01,970
A little bigger,

469
00:21:02,050 --> 00:21:05,010
but beyond a shadow of a doubt,
that was my real sister.

470
00:21:06,810 --> 00:21:08,730
Why's it like this?

471
00:21:08,810 --> 00:21:10,140
Damn it.

472
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:12,730
[birds chirping]

473
00:21:14,570 --> 00:21:18,530
Jin, if you're thinking of
putting a tail on 'em, drop it.

474
00:21:18,610 --> 00:21:19,900
Trust is imperative.

475
00:21:21,570 --> 00:21:22,870
Yes, it is.

476
00:21:24,330 --> 00:21:25,740
[GONZO] How troubling.

477
00:21:25,830 --> 00:21:28,450
He commands the Divine Guardians
Left and Right,

478
00:21:28,540 --> 00:21:30,500
which are meant to be held
by a third party

479
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:32,080
to check Break and Seal.

480
00:21:32,580 --> 00:21:35,090
But instead, that check is gone.

481
00:21:35,170 --> 00:21:36,550
And the inheritor of Seal

482
00:21:36,630 --> 00:21:38,840
holds far more power
than expected

483
00:21:38,920 --> 00:21:40,510
or was ever intended.

484
00:21:41,340 --> 00:21:43,380
If something happens
to young Yuru,

485
00:21:43,470 --> 00:21:45,600
there will be no one
to stop them.

486
00:21:47,140 --> 00:21:49,140
What would happen after that?

487
00:21:49,810 --> 00:21:51,640
Even I couldn't tell.

488
00:21:54,980 --> 00:21:57,440
[♪ closing theme song playing]

489
00:23:28,030 --> 00:23:30,910
[Right yells, laughs]

490
00:23:30,990 --> 00:23:33,040
[DERA]
Think they're Kagemori guys?

491
00:23:33,120 --> 00:23:34,790
[YURU] We're being followed.

492
00:23:34,870 --> 00:23:37,460
[GONZO] I'll just work you until
you wish you were dead!
